box} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32d0249e-396e-5abf-9c3e-a9a01870f500" :question/math-academy-id "q-161643" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4y>{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\n- **II.** $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\n- **III.** $∂A⊂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a380742f47d97062d56b482592cd2d2961dcc40262131a99886b815c507ab6e3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/26/26d264d702368ed6fe05577d7c34630bd16b41bdba8d206dd4db39763db02938.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊈A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and  II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3140a798-db1e-5f78-87be-0ad6910ccf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449970} {:answer/id #uuid "66652cf1-121a-55d6-b60b-7370a097e440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3140a798-db1e-5f78-87be-0ad6910ccf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449970} :answer-field/id #uuid "0239bed3-bff6-57a4-914e-a2a7696a453b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51696bef-50a4-5444-9a43-36db6f9afa18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449972} {:answer/id #uuid "42fe6b05-f33a-59cb-bdd4-1fe79fe94856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42fe6b05-f33a-59cb-bdd4-1fe79fe94856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449973} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fcaecef-8c7d-5939-af0c-a44de76b6473" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25836713-0be8-5121-b3d9-e6b2691cc476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449974} {:answer/id #uuid "d419b241-208a-5a0c-b5ad-26a22859c22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25836713-0be8-5121-b3d9-e6b2691cc476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449974} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f7ad3f5-382d-59a9-a467-493359e62446" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91207617-bfa9-5efa-a562-b7d640b0c541" :question/math-academy-id "q-161651" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=∂A\\cup \\text{int}A$\n- **II.** $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- **III.** $∂A⊂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a39ecae41a88e873fa9eecb30a5b554be9ec98cf630851715ab35f2f873710f2.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/5e/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and III are false. Since ${C}_{1}⊂∂A-A,$ we must have that $∂A⊄A$ and also that $A\\ne ∂A\\cup \\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb75