denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddcb03ab-ffc7-5dde-a933-7374df237b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449982} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3ecb14-3118-537c-b265-36ac3c5c4e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3ecb14-3118-537c-b265-36ac3c5c4e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449983} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db9f7f0-2fbe-5bfb-88f5-650ddb13358c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bbec439-5029-5663-98a6-7e32d79eaa0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449984} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e4b64f-bd71-5313-87a7-f6c616739ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9e4b64f-bd71-5313-87a7-f6c616739ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449985} :answer-field/id #uuid "300d5e5c-ad59-5480-a520-0c1afdf364a1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec3ff93-228e-542f-8812-a0b344b17573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449986} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9c77c6-5431-5dbf-9223-a1c8fe1ec4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9c77c6-5431-5dbf-9223-a1c8fe1ec4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449987} :answer-field/id #uuid "74c4ed37-cec0-5927-8a59-1ff0216677f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b9d32a6-dbbc-54ba-9b9d-46f810008dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161845" :question/problem "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function $f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a.$\n- **II.** The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n- **III.** The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the theorem, the function $f$ must be invertible in some neighborhood of $a.$\n\n- Statement II is also true. Indeed, the inverse ${f}^{-1}$ must be continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n\n- Statement III is also true. According to the theorem, we must have ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d65d348-380b-5f1a-8d6d-4fe1b2db6b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449988} {:answer/id #uuid "59c93832-fe98-545b-859c-ae8eb173bd4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d65d348-380b-5f1a-8d6d-4fe1b2db6b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449988} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd1bf69-489b-5265-9fa9-4746d265dca2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc47b583-9334-5b64-b2a1-d1741b28cf8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449990} {:answer/id #uuid "fe392d18-15aa-5a5b-9916-5395ad1e6647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe392d18-15aa-5a5b-9916-5395ad1e6647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449991} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0d3092d-28e8-5f0f-8af6-41deece82164" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450949} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c096ebcf-8397-5faf-9dd6-c2509fd106b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449992} {:answer/id #uuid "655d1d09-5adb-5ec9-b4bd-060d64f54341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655d1d09-5adb-5ec9-b4bd-060d64f54341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449993} :answer-field/id #uuid "bddffa24-0649-52c9-a5aa-e2628f8f7a10" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46fbce01-7db5-5630-8364-44d4a151bbf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-162346" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${w}^{4}+1=1$\n- **II.** ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1$\n- **III.** $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n{w}^{4}+1=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4} & =\\frac{{z}^{4}}{{w}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1,$ which means that $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the quotient of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d21fd0f3-61ca-55b8-992d-8caa336fbfe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449994} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3cb37a-0a0d-5ba0-8686-df40ab573c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d21fd0f3-61ca-55b8-992d-8caa336fbfe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449994} :answer-field/id #uuid "1310c1aa-028f-5307-8a9b-23867e91afa4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae485c08-a054-506e-b702-e021a9033658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449996} {:answer/id #uuid "5977334f-6d05-5c75-ab12-d528d65f25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5977334f-6d05-5c75-ab12-d528d65f25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449997} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cbb280b-5ca4-53e4-8eac-de7da419020a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6707a3db-6596-5e6d-9281-5b095bdf34a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449998} {:answer/id #uuid "19b1a7f5-a6d2-5a80-808e-8390fc639dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b1a7f5-a6d2-5a80-808e-8390fc639dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449999} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d8aaf5-f0f6-51e8-a03e-90aeb065f7a7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b77c81df-773f-534f-b1e3-2174eb2531c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-162347" :question/problem "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$\n- **II.** ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity\n- **III.** ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cba55a4b-f247-535c-9e49-fa2e8c2cdcdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450000} {:answer/id #uuid "e93d1625-d6c8-5fd7-b1f4-1422b448e402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e93d1625-d6c8-5fd7-b1f4-1422b448e402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f940e62-9613-5985-ad24-d69a320fcd23" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9838a96-9d28-5e6e-86ab-1e2df5d2dd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450002} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f9dfb2-aace-5204-aa68-9a6d39b1025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f9dfb2-aace-5204-aa68-9a6d39b1025b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450003} :answer-field/id #uuid "45127e67-9050-53d7-aa37-4528a5b9d664" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "958ca900-dd33-56fd-ae4b-202ef4468f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450004} {:answer/id #uuid "cca75b27-9e73-5231-8841-30d90c37c9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cca75b27-9e73-5231-8841-30d90c37c9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450005} :answer-field/id #uuid "4631cdd6-da5c-5378-87e3-d81dc85b8e48" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b299b05-4c26-5412-a581-f913a340d791" :question/math-academy-id "q-162348" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $8$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${z}^{8}=1$\n- **II.** $(zw)^{8}=1$\n- **III.** $zw$ is an $8$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $z$ and $w$ are $8$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{8}={w}^{8}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{8} & ={z}^{8}{w}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(zw)^{8}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is an $8$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :kno