nswer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41fda86a-2906-564e-874d-326e526da153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450011} :answer-field/id #uuid "facbe088-cd3d-5c74-a75a-2f688e42e0fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a65d62e-3083-571b-b429-c51c7b117795" :question/math-academy-id "q-162349" :question/problem "Let $z$ be an $8$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $({z}^{4})^{2}=-1$\n- **II.** ${z}^{4}$ is an $8$th root of unity\n- **III.** ${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({z}^{4})}^{2}={z}^{8}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{4})^{8} & =({z}^{8})^{4} \\\\  & =(1)^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a $8$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{4})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{4}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8098262b-8dd2-5624-9085-904625cfb887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450012} {:answer/id #uuid "565d1fea-c5a2-50c4-8fb6-b49214d1efd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8098262b-8dd2-5624-9085-904625cfb887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450012} :answer-field/id #uuid "018e94fa-5c72-5d74-bab6-124b7efe13f3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc737ac-0b5f-5ac2-afd0-362038549581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450014} {:answer/id #uuid "9ffcc792-724b-59e1-af60-c0c0de877e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cc737ac-0b5f-5ac2-afd0-362038549581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450014} :answer-field/id #uuid "582b02fd-0bcc-529d-8b3f-572e83f2bf1d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b212c483-4bfe-501f-bf62-1de29c58fb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450016} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa065e5-2d93-581d-b99a-30633ef12be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa065e5-2d93-581d-b99a-30633ef12be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450017} :answer-field/id #uuid "13783559-b35e-5150-b4f1-efb4a153ccd3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec73ee18-5d78-5b94-8905-bcb7e7e3a771" :question/math-academy-id "q-162350" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- **II.** $(zw)^{4}=0$\n- **III.** $zw$ is a $4$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{4} & ={z}^{4}{w}^{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have seen above that $(zw)^{4}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a05e4afb-d3f8-5d45-8cff-94491c015c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450018} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ecf89a-83b1-5400-ac93-8dcb9a12ada9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9ecf89a-83b1-5400-ac93-8dcb9a12ada9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450019} :answer-field/id #uuid "323f6009-65c0-5f1e-bfb4-e29af6ffa6f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "470ae2f3-d813-5467-a00b-1e65976aabcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450020} {:answer/id #uuid "362c8fda-2955-54a8-848b-306b145cabc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "362c8fda-2955-54a8-848b-306b145cabc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450021} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc13bc5-159a-5499-af0e-47dcfe3e2739" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450964} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0037f4d4-a7c7-535a-86c3-26dde47eab84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450022} {:answer/id #uuid "017941c4-8b78-585a-ac13-d3c49bc2ea32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0037f4d4-a7c7-535a-86c3-26dde47eab84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450022} :answer-field/id #uuid "b18b7e10-b3be-5e48-b985-19fcdd420bc9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6154f21e-3dc4-5e29-9ac5-5bb6e4c1043c" :question/math-academy-id "q-162351" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be cube roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${z}^{3}=1$\n- **II.** $(z+z)^{3}=8$\n- **III.** $w+w=2w$ is a cube root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $z$ and $w$ are cube roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{3}={w}^{3}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. We obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+z)^{3} & =(2z)^{3} \\\\  & ={2}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{3} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. From statement II, we have that $(w+w)^{3}=8\\ne 1,$ which means that $w+w=2w$ is *not* a cube root of unity. \n\nIn general, the sum of $n$th roots of unity is *not* an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2565e429-f9e8-565e-b79c-50c15a9cf5a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450024} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb21cc4-06a9-526d-84b6-4821caa2028c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2565e429-f9e8-565e-b79c-50c15a9cf5a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450024} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f939f45-128a-54ba-8d72-a98d26e3b22f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18017d9b-3f30-5878-a1f2-cf30974582cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450026} {:answer/id #uuid "cc934039-e64d-586d-ad5e-e9ed86abb7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc934039-e64d-586d-ad5e-e9ed86abb7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450027} :answer-field/id #uuid "00988493-fe63-52ff-a252-2f5fd32d0abb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab21a80-fc5b-5fa5-a158-a3451675cd67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450028} {:answer/id #uuid "c2411d49-0b1c-5e7b-92ce-18503f09d34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2411d49-0b1c-5e7b-92ce-18503f09d34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450029} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6b41c77-8fa2-5905-bcbd-bf1b82c295fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10662523-d7b1-54f8-907f-f332605eaff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-162368" :question/problem "Let $z$ be a $4$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- **II.** $(z+z)^{4}=16$\n- **III.** $z+z=2z$  is not a $4$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ is a  $4$th root of unity, then (by definition) we have that\n\n$$\n{z}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+z)^{4} & =(2z)^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{4} \\\\  & =16\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(z+z)^{4}\\ne 1,$ which means that $z+z=2z$ is *not* a $4$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Product and Quotient Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33261e2c-f530-55f6-9a1e-c48edf2dbfbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450030} {:answer/id #uuid "df43e443-d2ad-5cb2-838a-375dc9dd3ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33261e2c-f530-55f6-9a1e-c48edf2dbfbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450030} :answer-field/id #uuid "a18ffba7-727f-548e-a5e6-8765617e4156" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c17aeb28-10f7-5ea2-856b-799205f3ac1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450032} {:answer/id #uuid "adea7f39-7a82-5e30-b1bc-6d10303ac5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adea7f39-7a82-5e30-b1bc-6d10303ac5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450033} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ac4bac-ea62-5a8c-816e-baf4fd05d6ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450970} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca745289-b77c-5652-a598-01437a776c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450034} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb8db25-01e7-56a6-80c6-307dc1495238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca745289-b77c-5652-a598-01437a776c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450034} :answer-field/id #uuid "cac92ed1-bc20-55bc-9a9a-5a514bc44b7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b7bc6df-b3cb-50da-83fc-955ab52a05f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-162369" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $6$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $z{w}^{6}=w$\n- **II.** $(zw)^{6}=1$\n- **III.** $zw$ is not a $6$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,  since $z$ and $w$ are $6$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have\n\n$$\n{z}^{6}={w}^{6}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\nz{w}^{6}=z\\cdot 1=z\\ne w.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(zw)^{6} & ={z}^{6}{w}^{6} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have seen above that $(zw)^{6}=1,$ which means that $zw$ is a $6$th root of unity.  \n\nIn general, the product of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II  only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7c2d70-ba75-5ef8-9097-90bddc50b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450036} {:answer/id #uuid "8120d27e-6b2e-5bc7-b0d7-67a8bde31356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c7c2d70-ba75-5ef8-9097-90bddc50b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450036} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e48cef-ad68-54f9-ba61-c315918da173" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983c66ff-c84d-5db7-a81a-8e7b44a5fd0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450038} {:answer/id #uuid "99dcf27d-c822-58ad-ae4e-86be30e29f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99dcf27d-c822-58ad-ae4e-86be30e29f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450039} :answer-field/id #uuid "200056d3-b737-545d-a891-be7f2e1df5b6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450973} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f724c9d-ed07-57ad-b98a-93fd792e8837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450040} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d9d07f-d563-5a25-967e-56613d363fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7d9d07f-d563-5a25-967e-56613d363fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450041} :answer-field/id #uuid "9536bd2c-2cb7-5126-9d02-c69eb4ee5a13" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62a3796-3a93-54ec-8c55-9e54ca670215" :question/math-academy-id "q-162379" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $p(x)\\in N,$ where $p(x)={x}^{3}-1.$\n- **II.** For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$\n- **III.** The set is closed under addition." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have, $p(x)={x}^{3}-1\\notin N$ because\n\n$$\np(0)=(0)^{3}-1=-1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x),g(x)\\in N,$ where $f(0)=0$ and $g(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=0+0=0.\n$$\n\nHence $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baecaaf6-adc1-5d33-8bb8-faa4d72e9b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450042} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6d539e-41ec-53a4-a51e-3ac27752733a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baecaaf6-adc1-5d33-8bb8-faa4d72e9b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450042} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0a6dde1-6915-5386-9e54-09f03885a256" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4841091b-2e64-5984-821c-cc3100911960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450044} {:answer/id #uuid "4714431a-4c69-5d40-b0eb-f99202ac6ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4714431a-4c69-5d40-b0eb-f99202ac6ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450045} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2520d6-e623-58d6-b7c6-97e729a08a49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e9b0ff-d627-5567-9969-d7cee3aac65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450046} {:answer/id #uuid "b20b3572-1110-5d75-a050-ca0b765e2ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b20b3572-1110-5d75-a050-ca0b765e2ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450047} :answer-field/id #uuid "451e24a9-762f-57f2-bbfd-3d7dbb6ae449" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9060a6c-635e-5bea-91ee-1f014ee29783" :question/math-academy-id "q-162391" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant different from $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The  matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $S.$\n\n- **II.** For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n\n- **III.** For any $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have $A+(B-C)=(A+B)-C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with real entries,   there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice if $A\\in S$ then \n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot |A|=|A|\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in S,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+(B-C)=A+(B+(-C))=(A+B)+(-C)=(A+B)-C\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30bb7b96-0ee1-540e-a86d-287f27a702b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450048} {:answer/id #uuid "37ffb9ee-3671-538d-82eb-1a76ca7b6bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ffb9ee-3671-538d-82eb-1a76ca7b6bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450049} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e2d51bd-2585-5f79-94d3-b038a415082e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b0a5de1-ebdf-50db-b852-bdb9ce68a858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450050} {:answer/id #uuid "a60f5a43-04d9-5f88-b2bc-365bc6d9531d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b0a5de1-ebdf-50db-b852-bdb9ce68a858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450050} :answer-field/id #uuid "196f729e-b1a5-5503-a13d-a4964e7a82dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1997ce5d-b934-50cb-856c-b4aaa92fef20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450052} {:answer/id #uuid "a552e5a8-222c-522a-b522-815b9887824d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1997ce5d-b934-50cb-856c-b4aaa92fef20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450052} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6507d2c-9d83-5368-870c-3233d9d50c59" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b2f6345-ac14-55a4-a687-5a14893fcf90" :question/math-academy-id "q-162392" :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2},$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n\n- **II.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)-q(x)=q(x)-p(x).$\n\n- **III.** There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as \n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{3}+0\\cdot {x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \nHence, $0\\in U.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{3}\\in U$ and the zero-polynomial $q(x)=0\\in U.$ Then \n\n$$\np(x)-q(x)=p(x)-0={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\nq(x)-p(x)=0-p(x)=-{x}^{3}\\ne {x}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1934f404-12fe-5061-8332-ddf77cb3358c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450054} {:answer/id #uuid "74f484ed-f46c-525a-91d9-9aaef9742b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1934f404-12fe-5061-8332-ddf77cb3358c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450054} :answer-field/id #uuid "3459f397-effb-554b-8666-6e19befcd06c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af42c2a-0086-5f9d-b466-8f7cf82f0afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450056} {:answer/id #uuid "b8443a5b-debf-548f-b22a-c7ad859d5840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8443a5b-debf-548f-b22a-c7ad859d5840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450057} :answer-field/id #uuid "e741088c-ec60-5745-a82c-5940206acaae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5820bb4-4dd8-5a96-b849-4c1a4fe09b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450058} {:answer/id #uuid "d9479a5c-4388-57b2-95d8-85f7d1fd0876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5820bb4-4dd8-5a96-b849-4c1a4fe09b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450058} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ec5b6c-64cb-56f5-9f54-68b907247bdd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b6ba3e9-8414-5dea-8a72-007f56c21b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162530" :question/problem "The region $R$ is bounded between the cone $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and the paraboloid $x=\\sqrt{2y}.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,{g}_{1}(y)\\le z\\le {g}_{2}(y),\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}_{1}(y,z)=\\sqrt{2y}$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$\n- **II.** ${g}_{1}(y)=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and ${g}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$\n- **III.** $a=-1$ and $b=1$" :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional region of type II can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nLet's find a type II representation of our region.\n\n**Step 1.** We start by finding the surfaces ${f}_{1}(y,z)$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z).$ Since all $x$ in the region are bounded *below* by $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and *above* by $x=\\sqrt{2y},$ we have\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{1}(y,z)}\\le x\\le {{\\sqrt{2y}}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n**Step 2.** We find the projection of the intersection between the cone $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ and the paraboloid $x=\\sqrt{2y}$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nNotice that the equation of the cone is already solved for $x.$ Substituting this expression for $x$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{2y} \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =2y \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y+{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y+1+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the projection of the intersection is the circle $(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ centered at $(1,0)$ in the $yz$-plane. \n\n![](images/d6/d6db5f2d27787c5414f92c2525398b3810d0b0d192ea6837f7cdf483531f48e9.png)\n\nThe region is bounded *below* by $z=-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}$ and bounded *above* by $z=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{{-\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{{g}_{1}(y)}\\le z\\le {{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{{g}_{2}(y)}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\n**Step 3.** We find the bounds for $y.$ From the diagram, $y$ is bounded *below* by $y=0$ and bounded *above* by $y=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{{0}_{⏟}}_{a}\\le y\\le {{2}_{⏟}}_{b}.\n$$\n\nSo, statement III is false.\n\nFinally, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ab2b92-956a-5542-8558-9d8353d363f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450060} {:answer/id #uuid "eca73180-f340-5ba3-8d1c-1ba3a952c9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eca73180-f340-5ba3-8d1c-1ba3a952c9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450061} :answer-field/id #uuid "b102cea3-f562-5bbc-b248-b7fd89563d70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2924e9da-5763-50eb-bf48-93b44a58eaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450062} {:answer/id #uuid "25d328db-2634-516f-9952-32935f11ffe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25d328db-2634-516f-9952-32935f11ffe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450063} :answer-field/id #uuid "334fb609-34b8-512d-927b-a8ea1e632a29" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "768efe7b-ef20-53e5-a58a-44ad13d32eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450064} {:answer/id #uuid "381ee2c7-9797-5969-a87b-fe851ec6009e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768efe7b-ef20-53e5-a58a-44ad13d32eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450064} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee93e453-3d49-54de-9414-b1ecee02547b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ab2ad7f-5552-5a07-8645-8d079346b7d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162620" :question/problem "Let $G$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zero matrix $O=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $G.$\n- **II.** For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in G,$ we have $A-O=A.$\n- **III.** For any $A,B\\in G,$ we have $A-B=B-A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,$O=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]$ with $a=b=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, as for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\nA-O=A+(-O)=A+O=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, let's consider the matrices $O=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Then $O$ and ${I}_{2}$ belong to $G,$ and we\nhave \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}-O={I}_{2}\n$$\n\n \nbut \n\n$$\nO-{I}_{2}=-{I}_{2}\\ne {I}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2779fb-9930-5fcd-bcd1-7e1f1104d4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450066} {:answer/id #uuid "91b3e3fc-389a-585f-96b5-7db78750f42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b3e3fc-389a-585f-96b5-7db78750f42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450067} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7c9859-71fa-5115-a310-1182f4bf63bc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "662847ba-aeb6-5cbd-8649-2265e32224d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450068} {:answer/id #uuid "bf79e41d-5399-5862-8d64-f981b0f2cf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf79e41d-5399-5862-8d64-f981b0f2cf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450069} :answer-field/id #uuid "b083e9d7-fb4e-5c84-9a1a-a1c99a0f9d6c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450988} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69cd0a9e-9920-5b05-8ece-dcad3cae55ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450070} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7468af-0186-5e65-ab49-7c01cd3fc068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc7468af-0186-5e65-ab49-7c01cd3fc068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450071} :answer-field/id #uuid "b050593e-e59b-5bdf-835e-4f773eafb358" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff69a5c1-505a-5719-b6b9-7ec69e0931ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-162664" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\n- **II.** For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n\n- **III.** For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider the null function $f(x)=0=0{x}^{2}\\in Q.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot 0=0=f(x).\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6dc2795-4ab0-51de-a770-20d43c3a88f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450072} {:answer/id #uuid "06198632-4bef-5852-8df3-61b23cc71b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6dc2795-4ab0-51de-a770-20d43c3a88f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450072} :answer-field/id #uuid "76c5b6a9-c201-5cfe-94b7-0a5d6e2baf31" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554b7f4f-d75d-532f-af10-b13a3597fa28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450074} {:answer/id #uuid "39d14144-cd01-511c-b559-2f430b3240b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d14144-cd01-511c-b559-2f430b3240b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450075} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc461b09-0b94-5bf1-9079-3927e7dcb562" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5a4b91-36ef-5113-a4b9-d1f9b7d8da80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450076} {:answer/id #uuid "aa572e6a-aad9-513a-b665-99a85554378d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa572e6a-aad9-513a-b665-99a85554378d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450077} :answer-field/id #uuid "55832c01-3fed-5f96-9d33-cae8fdc270f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69e25145-91f1-58d1-afd8-be54a0c5863e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162665" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $2.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\in S$\n- **II.** For any $p(x)\\in S,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot p(x)\\in S$\n- **III.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $S$ contains only polynomials whose degree is at most $2.$ However, $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is *not* a polynomial. So, $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let $deg(q)$ the degree of a polynomial $q.$ Then, for any $p(x)\\in S$ we have that $(-1)\\cdot p(x)$ is also a polynomial, and that\n\n$$\ndeg((-1)\\cdot p)=deg(-1)+deg(p)=0+deg(p)\\le 2.\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)p(x)\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(x),q(x)\\in S$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the values $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c42ccdb6-b921-5da6-8d61-829338f9c0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450078} {:answer/id #uuid "2b082b3a-de73-5d72-8407-3ea0f366430e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b082b3a-de73-5d72-8407-3ea0f366430e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450079} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ded1d6-fd62-535d-a00c-5652c123a362" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b94594f5-40c0-57fa-a320-b6e74879d268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450080} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a33687-ca33-58d2-9263-d09f15df4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a33687-ca33-58d2-9263-d09f15df4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450081} :answer-field/id #uuid "e22d5ab6-389d-5f69-99dc-1d75e06d9f38" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45057e96-393e-5a76-b084-845e711d890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450082} {:answer/id #uuid "be6cad6a-51eb-557f-9298-7fa92791e5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45057e96-393e-5a76-b084-845e711d890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450082} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f084e17-158e-5d0d-b97b-c2a08151797a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2124447c-ee22-58ee-9afe-87a9532907c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162668" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices with determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $A\\in Y,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A=-A.$\n- **II.** For any $A\\in Y$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$\n- **III.** For any $A\\in Y$ we have $2A\\in Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot {a}_{ij}=-{a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot A=-A.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\in Y,$ however $2{I}_{2}\\notin Y$ because\n\n$$\n|2{I}_{2}|=|2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d58fba3c-4bbf-5a74-a911-18db101eb632" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Axis Lengths Given a Homogeneous Polynomial Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "345441f2-5087-5b4b-a170-90bd9b45c571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450084} {:answer/id #uuid "6254eb3a-73c1-5ab0-ad43-6689f0121fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6254eb3a-73c1-5ab0-ad43-6689f0121fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450085} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade2cdd4-1d37-5b7e-95ec-f1c1d23d5682" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39dcc466-ba2e-5602-ad92-d2b70dc0ca1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450086} {:answer/id #uuid "eef8513c-faf1-5a9c-bdee-f872e4aea8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39dcc466-ba2e-5602-ad92-d2b70dc0ca1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450086} :answer-field/id #uuid "25be7e84-c62f-5a39-8971-0aa1b7350b97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6047f0f-3255-59c4-8ede-45caac330c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450088} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1502e5-81a3-537f-95d3-b3d0727811dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6047f0f-3255-59c4-8ede-45caac330c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450088} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c2d7ce5-553e-5e2f-a362-c4933f79bc92" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0602fa5a-d2db-5bf8-9142-ab8253a6eb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-16562" :question/problem "Consider the ellipse whose equation is $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}–48x+72y+144=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Its center is $(6,-4)$\n- **II.** The length of the major axis is $6$\n- **III.** The length of the minor axis is $4$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}–48x+72y+144 & =0 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-48x)+(9{y}^{2}+72y)+144 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{2}-48x)+(9{y}^{2}+72y)+144 & =0 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-12x]+9[{y}^{2}+8y]+144 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-6)^{2}-{6}^{2}]+9[(y+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}]+144 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-6)^{2}-36]+9[(y+4)^{2}-16]+144 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-6)^{2}-144+9(y+4)^{2}-144+144 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-6)^{2}-144+9(y+4)^{2}-144+144 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-6)^{2}+9(y+4)^{2} & =-144+144+144 \\\\ 4(x-6)^{2}+9(y+4)^{2} & =144 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $6>4,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 6=12,$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the ellipse is centered at $(6,-4).$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, statements II and III are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d58fba3c-4bbf-5a74-a911-18db101eb632" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Axis Lengths Given a Homogeneous Polynomial Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2957afb5-8dcc-5a3c-be47-05cd7087772b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450090} {:answer/id #uuid "fa300c46-2e42-5e26-904d-c234a85fedd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa300c46-2e42-5e26-904d-c234a85fedd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450091} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ebc973-6cfc-5de6-929b-112f67a157b8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7be024a6-037e-5a9c-8731-7ee43c421778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450092} {:answer/id #uuid "4da959f1-cca3-58ea-9511-04f4035a7d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7be024a6-037e-5a9c-8731-7ee43c421778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450092} :answer-field/id #uuid "199799b9-038e-5a89-b4fd-5681ab30823f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfa900cf-a600-5125-b96f-9228d0ef5991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450094} {:answer/id #uuid "ece15639-1727-5187-966a-fffa729d12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ece15639-1727-5187-966a-fffa729d12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450095} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f5c4b2-643a-5f2f-b14b-8553d388fa54" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f98a559b-0a7a-50c5-b65c-b026bdee915b" :question/math-academy-id "q-16639" :question/problem "Consider the ellipse whose equation is $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-9=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Its center is $(0,0)$\n- **II.** The length of the major axis is $3$\n- **III.** The length of the minor axis is $2\\sqrt{3}$" :question/worked-solution "We rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $3>\\sqrt{3},$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 3=6,$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the ellipse is centered at $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018101f5-88ee-578c-a18f-ccb93c8d48a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450096} {:answer/id #uuid "c29f7788-c13c-5a54-a0c1-b9bc3632f0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c29f7788-c13c-5a54-a0c1-b9bc3632f0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450097} :answer-field/id #uuid "a15ee7f8-704f-50c7-a501-7e31a8a48730" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451002} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fc1dfdb-574a-5d3e-8dcc-d5d199f77133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450098} {:answer/id #uuid "44ee64b7-a9ed-57a5-9c6d-f5b74d0c9d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fc1dfdb-574a-5d3e-8dcc-d5d199f77133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450098} :answer-field/id #uuid "8404deb2-95c0-5b00-b0a4-3ba4ca1fd885" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451003} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b9611-610d-526d-aa04-e5f83ac6ed51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450100} {:answer/id #uuid "a5e22063-362d-5058-bb98-b1bcb42d4106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061b9611-610d-526d-aa04-e5f83ac6ed51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450100} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7fdbc26-d6af-51af-bd0e-f6efec58fa66" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "044de50e-6da8-5a08-93e7-4cbfebd23610" :question/math-academy-id "q-177658" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838c5084-eb44-519f-a803-5a82f181e56f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450102} {:answer/id #uuid "21d2ed10-202f-51b3-ba91-671ffa3044b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21d2ed10-202f-51b3-ba91-671ffa3044b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450103} :answer-field/id #uuid "258cc04b-5017-5949-824f-ec823acf6383" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0826a009-00f9-5adc-bce5-6f9fcda95294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450104} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c513a9-75b1-5961-9a3b-199d701df809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1c513a9-75b1-5961-9a3b-199d701df809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450105} :answer-field/id #uuid "067e8cef-a0a9-5385-8882-0f661b4be518" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9638414-3798-5f91-a1d3-e5e7f0eb46de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450106} {:answer/id #uuid "0496a90c-d5f1-5c68-8740-345ff17ec22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0496a90c-d5f1-5c68-8740-345ff17ec22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450107} :answer-field/id #uuid "925d9be4-b3e2-57f7-969e-84df3d94eb40" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d52fcd7c-0cb8-5f3b-83e6-5d87eafb229f" :question/math-academy-id "q-177660" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1a953a-f5cc-5be1-84b3-69be0a7afa05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450108} {:answer/id #uuid "64c1ca58-d0a7-51aa-9436-360d901fce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64c1ca58-d0a7-51aa-9436-360d901fce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450109} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bed3038-b384-5d43-92b5-a0801e084f7f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387af6f7-f068-535a-b1fa-30498114a5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450110} {:answer/id #uuid "d52bca8f-a9d5-5566-ae77-cab60157a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d52bca8f-a9d5-5566-ae77-cab60157a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450111} :answer-field/id #uuid "969e4688-8a93-5b23-94b5-256f6e748b85" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c9c179-5409-5d04-9678-f54cfceb9c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450112} {:answer/id #uuid "71370e63-41c6-524f-82b0-a8ba1bdc4344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71370e63-41c6-524f-82b0-a8ba1bdc4344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450113} :answer-field/id #uuid "60bc5925-c6b8-5b12-a3d1-f7e96566501c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c17d5c10-3940-55d7-92e1-ac427e80f858" :question/math-academy-id "q-177662" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b83cbcb7-0b07-5ebc-aa53-89e2be0b52df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450114} {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115} :answer-field/id #uuid "f129ca4a-c8e7-580b-91d4-1a0d29e6e4ed" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} {:answer/id #uuid "72a3e0ac-77bc-591c-8e67-8888858b7e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} :answer-field/id #uuid "e642ba26-55cc-5b02-a022-90bbe00ce622" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} {:answer/id #uuid "990655aa-5186-5262-8a17-20c96c8aacfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d44e42c-bf19-521c-a0c4-c2026051681e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ef1bd48-9355-501c-9dc0-0c7250b226e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-177663" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d97560d4-a461-56ad-a02a-6185cd8091f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450120} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3bb08d-8578-5b00-b629-ee493e1578e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97560d4-a461-56ad-a02a-6185cd8091f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450120} :answer-field/id #uuid "449a008c-d031-5728-9ddb-18ed8015f4e0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451014} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35e6176-6e61-538b-b777-81081565e782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450122} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ec417-5580-56cf-9c8b-fca4b581b7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c35e6176-6e61-538b-b777-81081565e782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450122} :answer-field/id #uuid "245ee836-a023-59ec-b707-2ff0dcbaae25" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 175921864