92186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55b1acd6-5df7-5bc0-a3b3-0f00f1d5d19b" :question/math-academy-id "q-182018" :question/problem "For the sets $X={f,g,h}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(f,g)\\in Z$\n- **II.** $(f,g,h)\\in Z$\n- **III.** $(h,h)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/17/1718bd6f3f2eaa8dd8fe581b0d938b3b5f1928d5e56a11a324f145e7a481fabe.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(f,f),(f,g),(f,h),(g,f),(g,g),(g,h),(h,f),(h,g),(h,h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91f809ca-0f0e-5928-aaf3-75099caebdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450138} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6343da-43d1-5e19-91dd-f701db7355f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91f809ca-0f0e-5928-aaf3-75099caebdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450138} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b97fb6a-64fc-5b59-add5-c689202db96b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2dbf9d4-9ad4-57b6-b96a-e243ae870a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450140} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e15bdc-8f44-59b2-b3ec-e802a5e7f88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2dbf9d4-9ad4-57b6-b96a-e243ae870a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450140} :answer-field/id #uuid "884c8d4a-6f52-53b7-810f-2251c4404eaf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df2ed952-f0e1-5e6c-a0a6-9b589866ab36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450142} {:answer/id #uuid "28327767-1cdb-597b-b632-877d2ba8eb44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28327767-1cdb-597b-b632-877d2ba8eb44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450143} :answer-field/id #uuid "7febc880-96fc-5ce8-9259-58520b401afb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06e30e6f-bad6-5263-b9ac-ef88aa63ab32" :question/math-academy-id "q-182021" :question/problem "For the sets $X={k,m,n}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${k}^{2}\\in Z$\n- **II.** $(k,n,m)\\in Z$\n- **III.** $(m,n)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/e7/e7c24108e0d9f5e2e7edbfbe90cdf7318bc247aa73a4c9c72dc61449c7b4da94.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(k,k),(k,m),(k,n),(m,k),(m,m),(m,n),(n,k),(n,m),(n,n)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3e965e-0ede-5794-8234-d689c265775d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450144} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e314c9-8d13-5929-9288-d0b03caee001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c3e965e-0ede-5794-8234-d689c265775d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450144} :answer-field/id #uuid "756a7bdb-06ea-559c-9584-67d8e010a4a2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6004589-36a3-5605-9d65-30a2ada9e5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450146} {:answer/id #uuid "aeda2d75-6c00-556c-9957-42f13ce55279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeda2d75-6c00-556c-9957-42f13ce55279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450147} :answer-field/id #uuid "945a6a3e-d94f-50cf-8e24-4848ae5c81be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd89201-5db8-5ed7-9cc2-e7a46271275a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450148} {:answer/id #uuid "ed455369-3605-5412-ae71-53798de31af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed455369-3605-5412-ae71-53798de31af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450149} :answer-field/id #uuid "1717e3d3-9478-5662-b4b2-f6094bbc21fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a71b6cc-f717-587b-ac69-3fbfad95bd60" :question/math-academy-id "q-182022" :question/problem "For the sets $Z=\\{-3,6,-9\\}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,6,-3)\\in Y$\n\n- **II.** $(-3,-9)\\in Y$\n\n- **III.** $(-9,6)\\in Y$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/0c/0c58bf1f025cc4960ce3b9dc8e1bc3bf474a521473833b27d136fd77fd6b814a.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(-3,-3),(-3,6),(-3,-9),(6,-3),(6,6),(6,-9),(-9,-3)(-9,6),(-9,-9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e93fd7f-070f-5359-aabb-cba5cc275015" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent or Divergent Integrals With Unbounded Limits"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6714027-f7d1-59ad-bb4a-3c0caaceb7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450150} {:answer/id #uuid "43c1f7c7-58cb-5a34-b9e1-00de3b40522d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6714027-f7d1-59ad-bb4a-3c0caaceb7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450150} :answer-field/id #uuid "282dd84c-885a-5d3c-8892-249c5ac358c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3c3f58-0b39-5bd2-9b22-7075ff9caf50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450152} {:answer/id #uuid "0cdc461c-f756-54a7-ab52-ca95ca7b7286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cdc461c-f756-54a7-ab52-ca95ca7b7286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450153} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20765af-d652-51f5-8526-88fd000fa80e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451030} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5452b9a-a0d4-5a70-9145-3d1900a8348a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450154} {:answer/id #uuid "a6df44a6-2fd6-56e4-b156-51e57d7aa00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6df44a6-2fd6-56e4-b156-51e57d7aa00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450155} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb1d552d-6c85-5168-a4c5-f67edd8762c4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "176fa3e2-797b-5eec-aaaa-e654fc774ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20788" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi x+1).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is convergent\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an improper integral in which both the left and right endpoints are unbounded:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIf the integrand $f(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ then we can break the integral up into two improper integrals, each with a single unbounded endpoint:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we can compute each of the two integrals separately and combine their results. \n\n**Watch out!** If either of the two integrals on the right-hand side is divergent, then the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent.\n\nLet's evaluate each integral in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{5\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi x+1){|}_{0}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi a+1)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs $a\\to \\infty $, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi a+1)$ oscillates between $-1$ and $1.$ So the integral diverges.\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{5\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi x+1){|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\pi }{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi x+1)].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs $a\\to -\\infty $, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi x+1)$ oscillates between $-1$ and $1.$ So the integral diverges.\n\n- Statement III is true. The integral in statement III can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHowever, both integrals on the right-hand side are divergent. Therefore, the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent.\n\nIn conclusion,  only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69c09760-2d64-5dc1-bd95-dbf93b49b75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450156} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb90533-2e1f-508d-a49f-33cb04df8165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb90533-2e1f-508d-a49f-33cb04df8165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450157} :answer-field/id #uuid "352f6126-fd80-562e-ba27-8dfb9087ceab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1840414b-3944-5796-ad10-fefa18374ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450158} {:answer/id #uuid "f592a2fd-2ad2-5a64-b1a1-518ee0502f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f592a2fd-2ad2-5a64-b1a1-518ee0502f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450159} :answer-field/id #uuid "9362b5d3-3ec4-5533-9758-c6204cf9b6e0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a31074-4dac-5fd9-8605-009d13ebe2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450160} {:answer/id #uuid "8df65c50-3dc4-5365-8556-462f00971dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a31074-4dac-5fd9-8605-009d13ebe2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450160} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c12c083-9778-5df4-89ea-8b2c7152665c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e9580a2-179f-5d46-9d50-b4d9da5c57d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20976" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $45$\n- **II.** The global minimum value is $-14$\n- **III.** The global maximum value is $18$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)-(x+2) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-2,\\,-1,\\,1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3(-2)^{4}+8(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)+5=13 \\\\ f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}+8(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-24(-1)+5=18 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}+8(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-24(1)+5=-14 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)^{4}+8(2)^{3}-6(2)^{2}-24(2)+5=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=45,$ so the global maximum is $45.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=-14,$ so the global minimum is $-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\n![](images/9b/9b48417439d0e018250328b92561732dd9f4c8bbec157daf33287b20dac7c41f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" :knowledge-point/title "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5285eae7-b173-5c81-8d86-d6fb4a673467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450162} {:answer/id #uuid "29f89acb-432c-5acb-8c55-8e8f6545caf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5285eae7-b173-5c81-8d86-d6fb4a673467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450162} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc345bec-1471-5cef-bc81-64c8cc550ae4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b4bf8b-2198-50c1-8ec5-1869900a28d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450164} {:answer/id #uuid "d7007cf9-a8d6-5da1-a069-7bc629eae345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7007cf9-a8d6-5da1-a069-7bc629eae345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450165} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6001636-c752-5590-a7ce-9993d6e6c855" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f3eaf5-d90c-58a3-9efc-4d7d25551712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450166} {:answer/id #uuid "456e91f8-d14f-5029-ab0c-333e4c482c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "456e91f8-d14f-5029-ab0c-333e4c482c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450167} :answer-field/id #uuid "85269cee-331a-5495-bd44-a2a82eb9b161" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89e4e3cf-d4a8-5dba-b035-5946e9d4ce09" :question/math-academy-id "q-20979" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=13-9{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3},$ on the interval $[-1,2],$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $2$\n- **II.** The global maximum value is $13$\n- **III.** The global minimum value is $-7$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=13-9{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-18x+6{x}^{2} \\\\  & =6x(x-3),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n6x(x-3)=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,3.\n$$\n\nSince $x=3$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,2]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =13-9(-1)^{2}+2(-1)^{3}=2 \\\\ f(0) & =13-9(0)^{2}+2(0)^{3}=13 \\\\ f(2) & =13-9(2)^{2}+2(2)^{3}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=13,$ so the global maximum is $13.$\n\n- The least value is $f(2)=-7,$ so the global minimum is $-7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](images/1a/1a9d2f0db241c0a209c315a8e901e40a44258f339bbaa7bee36198b58fe2684d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da249f6-f00b-57cd-89a5-d251a642e06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450168} {:answer/id #uuid "0e057d4c-b3af-5161-859f-47a6b8967149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da249f6-f00b-57cd-89a5-d251a642e06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450168} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d3af8f1-2aec-5014-81ef-3189cc22782f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e799647-e810-5fe2-aa0f-f54e419579b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450170} {:answer/id #uuid "610235f4-8ef3-56cc-8749-bc3b4814b9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "610235f4-8ef3-56cc-8749-bc3b4814b9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450171} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7cf1057-4fd6-5565-8201-8f2730e1442d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e43f34a-e856-51d9-a5c3-5e8b65dece7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450172} {:answer/id #uuid "571bc3e9-d02c-53a5-bce2-0be868e001cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e43f34a-e856-51d9-a5c3-5e8b65dece7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450172} :answer-field/id #uuid "23fbed40-fb4d-5635-8cf9-cb424ea95e6b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b62475b-9e34-5901-b3b2-252278026eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450174} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbf4583-b589-56d5-8170-cf22b2ea39cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dbf4583-b589-56d5-8170-cf22b2ea39cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3621510-26a4-5dc7-bb5c-09395f6b5aac" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1676c625-f838-58d0-a1ed-b9b72fc63c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-20982" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **III.** ${f}^{″}(1)>0$\n- **IV.** $x=1$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4x,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{3}+4x & =0 \\\\ -4x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -4x(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-12{x}^{2}+4,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-8<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =4>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statement I is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=-1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false while statement IV is true. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105709 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33965139-0c6a-50fc-993a-e2acd6760212" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Local Minima and Local Maxima of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b1a512-445c-54f7-98eb-16e279f4f895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450176} {:answer/id #uuid "25b75876-10e0-5cad-a903-a2b32d7bf8db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b75876-10e0-5cad-a903-a2b32d7bf8db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450177} :answer-field/id #uuid "866a13a4-47ef-589e-9287-4ecfb3752c32" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec6ba65a-d7ef-5a8b-9423-07c0be64f56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450178} {:answer/id #uuid "42a6b76c-7760-543f-a116-629e13103e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42a6b76c-7760-543f-a116-629e13103e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450179} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a9c080-f207-5bcb-a51b-c9d90694422f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a9b19a-2378-558a-aaba-669f8e9eab83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450180} {:answer/id #uuid "a83dc05d-fde3-56f2-a463-d124bd96c060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a9b19a-2378-558a-aaba-669f8e9eab83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450180} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eca5308-cf1b-50be-902b-cb69f775f6b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d001b69-269c-523e-bfae-f0f86907fed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-21467" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-12x+6,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-2$ is a local maximum\n- **II.** $x=1$ is a local minimum\n- **III.** $x=1$ is a local maximum" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =6{x}^{2}+6x-12 \\\\  & =6({x}^{2}+x-2) \\\\  & =6(x+2)(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x+2)(x-1)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-2$ and $x=1.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-3,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-3) & =6(-3+2)(-3-1)=24>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =6(0+2)(0-1)=-12<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =6(2+2)(2-1)=24>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $-2$ | $(-2,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-3$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-2,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=-2$ is a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=1,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=1$ is a local minimum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff7c597d-d4a4-5567-add6-eac77475b0d6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Are Neither Local Minima nor Local Maxima"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7f0634-61fd-5c82-88da-7e629117634a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450182} {:answer/id #uuid "899d8517-fc94-54d3-9ecb-f90896d7de46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899d8517-fc94-54d3-9ecb-f90896d7de46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450183} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec9d5e27-2edf-590b-89a2-5622f244e8c1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c3829bd-23f7-5558-ad2d-ad25aa7aa625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450184} {:answer/id #uuid "f83818b6-de85-5ed1-a6ea-fd4bc327eefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f83818b6-de85-5ed1-a6ea-fd4bc327eefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450185} :answer-field/id #uuid "7522a75c-221f-5f7e-ba8d-0b0b878f71a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aac2952-926a-57ab-ba80-e57e635b4afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450186} {:answer/id #uuid "43d49d7f-c711-5838-b3c3-f67c7b4e70b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aac2952-926a-57ab-ba80-e57e635b4afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450186} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d5a316-4f26-5f0a-a784-27dddbbf543e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a70a3cbd-ee1f-54d1-83af-a484013d0e65" :question/math-academy-id "q-21468" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x)=4{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}+9,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-\\frac{3}{4}$ is a local minimum\n- **II.** $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum\n- **III.** $x=0$ is a local minimum" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=16{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}=4{x}^{2}(4x+3).\n$$\n\nAnd now find the stationary points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}(4x+3)=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,0.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,-\\frac{1}{2},1$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =4(-1)^{2}(4(-1)+3)=-4<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =4{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}(4(-\\frac{1}{2})+3)=1>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =4(1)^{2}(4+3)=28>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-\\frac{3}{4})$ | $-\\frac{3}{4}$ | $(-\\frac{3}{4},0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |  | $1$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |  | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-\\frac{3}{4},$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3}{4}$ is a local minimum.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7695c96f-227a-5a24-96bb-98331d20ed25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450188} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b00ef5-2972-5565-9c8d-615fbdea7d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6b00ef5-2972-5565-9c8d-615fbdea7d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450189} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec86aea-204a-537c-9265-e24eb853fbf5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "785b1360-8ef3-5e3d-bc20-b0fa4b4d9c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450190} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b54aef-16cd-5fa9-9ea9-5c40120eab94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b54aef-16cd-5fa9-9ea9-5c40120eab94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450191} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b01ba8-63a0-5562-83db-23726480b102" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285c8dc9-6285-500a-896b-acd2bd30c459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450192} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5e14c1-c34c-5064-bc85-8deb3ffd3502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "285c8dc9-6285-500a-896b-acd2bd30c459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450192} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cbc9b4-055f-5e80-834a-95af75ee5fe0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a459992-6292-5256-9176-368a35c4e9be" :question/math-academy-id "q-21498" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x-5.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(-2)>0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-2$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=-2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x-5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x+8.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb107d48-ade8-59ec-9f3f-9647d1dd8ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450194} {:answer/id #uuid "0e6a7f11-143b-5dad-9fa8-26bd5aa3ba78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb107d48-ade8-59ec-9f3f-9647d1dd8ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450194} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d2ae416-dab6-56f3-853a-13a41bcd30e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d51b7c1f-845e-5f42-ae9f-87a5ad90b535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450196} {:answer/id #uuid "25bbe643-d2a8-5ad9-b37b-6925f5785413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25bbe643-d2a8-5ad9-b37b-6925f5785413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450197} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5abbe1-37bc-59ba-97ad-66d356b8e172" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9923f078-f81a-53c2-8593-cbccad0915dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450198} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3b6fd7-2573-50bb-83e7-54096e8ece0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9923f078-f81a-53c2-8593-cbccad0915dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450198} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f205e1-a0a5-59f2-ad75-3388b2ab0d1e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cf080c3-6e5f-55a7-a304-f18da95a7022" :question/math-academy-id "q-21508" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6x-6.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5af6d2ba-7e1f-59a1-83fe-8e1adb7b24b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450200} {:answer/id #uuid "59750fcf-5216-5ec2-a1ec-d9fb69d7a2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5af6d2ba-7e1f-59a1-83fe-8e1adb7b24b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450200} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd903065-3e98-5220-b193-4510ce250e18" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "231ba120-c2fc-529e-b8bf-524707e79c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450202} {:answer/id #uuid "262fdf04-b5c2-5cda-bbee-46e634415301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "231ba120-c2fc-529e-b8bf-524707e79c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450202} :answer-field/id #uuid "2209190f-4473-571e-944d-2c7d7e504c9b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86164420-57eb-5080-ad56-a6c4dd3dfb66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450204} {:answer/id #uuid "475760e2-dc89-5c56-9260-157e83291c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475760e2-dc89-5c56-9260-157e83291c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450205} :answer-field/id #uuid "0decbc9b-2968-5888-808b-97ff28443d31" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14b8225f-a48c-5dd7-8177-203eb95c183f" :question/math-academy-id "q-21521" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+24x-36.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(4)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(4)>0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=4$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=4$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+24x-36,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+24.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(4) & =-3(4) \\\\  & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7229e4f-1a0f-5138-9a45-6dc29bc830bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450206} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e0c611-367a-55c4-8475-eddd7b148fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7229e4f-1a0f-5138-9a45-6dc29bc830bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450206} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf07852-9be5-5b6e-a12b-c3b51b0a4fe7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d87f9b0-eeb1-5185-a505-5bc778993df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450208} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe62dbe-512d-5b13-9d50-e60dfce14dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe62dbe-512d-5b13-9d50-e60dfce14dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450209} :answer-field/id #uuid "865d82c6-33c6-59af-8844-f035ceb3e2a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b4ef86-f69a-51e6-926b-39be08ff7785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450210} {:answer/id #uuid "4c846998-989f-5081-91e7-471e8cd1b1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02b4ef86-f69a-51e6-926b-39be08ff7785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450210} :answer-field/id #uuid "50dfdb87-b4cd-5a47-82f6-4a6c684b7414" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb8f5179-5e18-5e4e-a1cb-1566ffe5da1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-21536" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12{x}^{2}-12x+2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =12(1)^{2}-12(1)+2 \\\\  & =2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a173d2bb-a6d0-55c0-ad6c-1a58c9ab8da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450212} {:answer/id #uuid "949115a8-52b2-59e7-a41c-27c119276413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "949115a8-52b2-59e7-a41c-27c119276413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450213} :answer-field/id #uuid "44ca7820-6d41-551d-a79b-65f6050bd2e4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01ddae9-b073-55fa-ae34-870a6f063c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450214} {:answer/id #uuid "37a6e913-689c-58e3-97b3-b21ca71ab6c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b01ddae9-b073-55fa-ae34-870a6f063c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450214} :answer-field/id #uuid "24a3d678-7c46-5db8-b51c-5df7c09f1740" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c94ee2d-3972-57b4-bf31-f0632abdace0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450216} {:answer/id #uuid "65dd89d8-e402-5203-96cf-3c51d35a911d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65dd89d8-e402-5203-96cf-3c51d35a911d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450217} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f065d4b-9a26-5fcb-b19f-3bc754c9ebea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f189f1ac-fb45-57eb-b495-98b85aa3c2fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-21541" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3}.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{5})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5})<0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=\\frac{1}{5}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=-2{x}^{5/3}+{x}^{2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{10}{3}{x}^{2/3}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-1/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{20}{9}{x}^{-1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}{x}^{-4/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{5}) & =-\\frac{20}{9}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot {5}^{4/3}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {5}^{1/3}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8102373d-5a4e-5ac0-afc4-f3aae68224ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450218} {:answer/id #uuid "1761c082-eafb-55d7-b49c-28874b3df58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1761c082-eafb-55d7-b49c-28874b3df58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450219} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cea3bee-c05a-5d89-8ab4-89dbb7733e47" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e6bc632-6884-5271-8ebb-a732da326a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450220} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf65892-1cdc-5850-a956-c757558a3c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdf65892-1cdc-5850-a956-c757558a3c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450221} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2b62b6d-a089-56e5-aef7-7b85f39d0588" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc1397da-7168-5428-90a9-9874726b6e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450222} {:answer/id #uuid "88812dc1-d6f0-5b6c-b247-6aa1c6229a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88812dc1-d6f0-5b6c-b247-6aa1c6229a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450223} :answer-field/id #uuid "2abd71a2-9c62-5fe9-aad6-891ced37e599" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4b3d310-bdf5-54d8-92ee-e1b14c67f2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450224} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ab1cc3-fdee-5c80-8b2b-d73737bd570f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4b3d310-bdf5-54d8-92ee-e1b14c67f2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450224} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e40f01d-8407-51d5-8697-d3072f402e26" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61b494fc-0eab-5116-8219-a073a0f43da5" :question/math-academy-id "q-21812" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **III.** ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- **IV.** $x=1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12x-12{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-12{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12x(1-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12-24x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =12>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I and II are true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1a085da-c462-51a8-93d3-1eb3aae4d9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450226} {:answer/id #uuid "0cdad279-f642-5085-b9aa-5bcfaae95ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cdad279-f642-5085-b9aa-5bcfaae95ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450227} :answer-field/id #uuid "e07613ce-0ea6-5b64-9527-86d4b9a5c54f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80a14a0b-c634-507a-a4c5-cc06139bf258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450228} {:answer/id #uuid "d991e0ee-89a6-5974-93ac-7ed066b1c1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80a14a0b-c634-507a-a4c5-cc06139bf258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450228} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f3778f3-6efb-52a4-98ce-a667931dd927" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3fea93-af60-5f3d-b7fb-3dd859ef74ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450230} {:answer/id #uuid "7efdb310-fc36-5867-8fda-aa079eff2676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7efdb310-fc36-5867-8fda-aa079eff2676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450231} :answer-field/id #uuid "73e3e003-e861-50db-b033-d253d9b66dc2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ff51ed3-057d-5897-84bb-eff08d8a8619" :question/math-academy-id "q-21814" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=4{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}-20x+30.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(-1)<0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=-1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=4{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}-20x+30,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=20({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-x-1).\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20(4{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =20(4(-1)^{3}+3(-1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =20(-4+3-1) \\\\  & =-40<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7548774-130f-5f63-baf4-6274976c9d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450232} {:answer/id #uuid "7df2c0be-ed31-58c3-aa88-11e1bf4b26bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df2c0be-ed31-58c3-aa88-11e1bf4b26bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450233} :answer-field/id #uuid "8551b225-38de-593e-bdc7-5a16f6d4df25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd1ead83-e4dc-5bc5-85b7-260296d34c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450234} {:answer/id #uuid "39caab2e-6991-5e98-8e3e-0621eba51c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd1ead83-e4dc-5bc5-85b7-260296d34c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450234} :answer-field/id #uuid "64eaefcc-65cb-5c46-a620-f1b9260e0461" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64446a70-f505-5fdf-a194-43112cac8429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450236} {:answer/id #uuid "4fad96ff-d973-578b-9277-1a8feb412626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64446a70-f505-5fdf-a194-43112cac8429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450236} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c61787-c549-56d2-9a62-c81c8a6e0f43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ef7541b-0896-51b1-9ada-d5d0e26f455c" :question/math-academy-id "q-22007" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x+3.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(2)=0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=2$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}-12x+12.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=6x-12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =6\\cdot 2-12=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-12x+12 & =0 \\\\ 3(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=2.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=1,3$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}-12(1)+12=3>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-12(3)+12=3>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=2$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
